# Arabic Buzz — Project Rules

## Stack

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Shadcn UI patterns
- **Hosting:** Netlify via OpenNext / `@netlify/plugin-nextjs` runtime
- **AI:** Vercel AI SDK (`ai`) + OpenRouter / Google / OpenAI providers
- **Data:** PostgreSQL (Prisma / Supabase), env-only secrets

## Text & language

- Root layout **always** uses `lang="ar"` and `dir="rtl"`
- Font: `IBM_Plex_Sans_Arabic` from `next/font/google`
- All UI copy in **Modern Standard Arabic (MSA)**
- Code, JSON, URLs, and mono blocks must use `dir="ltr"` (and `className="ltr"` / logical Tailwind where needed)

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<html lang="ar" dir="rtl">
  <pre dir="ltr" className="font-mono">{json}</pre>
</html>

// ❌ BAD — LTR page chrome or Arabic inside unscoped mono without dir="ltr"
```

## Netlify deployment constraints

- Every `app/api/**/route.ts` must export:

```ts
export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'
```

- **Never** hardcode API keys, tokens, or webhook secrets
- Read secrets only from `process.env` (Netlify Environment Variables UI / `.env.local` locally)
- Prefer `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` only for non-secret client values (e.g. `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`)

## Agent / product conventions

- Preserve existing RTL workspace shell, scopes, HITL approvals, and SDAIA audit patterns
- Sensitive actions go through RBAC (`lib/auth/rbac.ts`) before execution
- Do not invent legal/tax facts; ground answers in RAG / provided sources when available
